fix(mcp): drop a default no call can reach (#215, #241)

The translation defaulted its projects mount when the field was empty, and the
branch-coverage gate caught that the empty case is never taken: 44 times false,
never true.

It cannot be taken. Both ways a configuration reaches the tool — the installer
and the environment fallback — set the mount before anything can call in, which
is why containerPath beside it reads the field directly rather than defaulting
too. So the branch was not a missing test, it was a claim about the code that no
call could make true.

Removed rather than covered. A test written to reach it would have had to build
a configuration the tool cannot be in, and would then assert on behaviour that
never happens.

